a. provide education on reproductive health, religious values, and moral values;
b. social rehabilitation;
c. psychosocial assistance during treatment until recovery; and
d. provide protection and assistance at every level of examination starting from investigation, prosecution, up to examination in court proceedings.

Article 70
(1) Health recovery services as referred to in Article 66 paragraph (2) letter d number 1 include: a. emergency services;
b. services for the provision of visum et repertum or visum psychiatricum in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. follow-up services in the form of outpatient and/or inpatient care in accordance with medical provisions;
d. deoxyribose nucleic acid verification services;
e. delivery process services for pregnancy as a result of sexual violence and/or rape;
f. services for the provision of further referrals in accordance with the circumstances and condition of the victim; and
g. services for the provision of special rooms separated from general patients.
(2) The OPD that handles health affairs is obligated to organize the provision of health recovery services.

